      "note": [
        "Statistical methods is used to protect the data of individuals in the statistics presented. For this reason, the presented totals do not always equal the sum of their reported components. See also section 2.2.6 Model assumptions in the quality declaration documentation on Statistics Sweden’s website.",
        "Individuals with a self-sufficient income below three income base amounts in a year are classified as non-self-sufficient. However, full-time students or conscripts with a self-sufficient income below three income base amounts are not included in the non-self-sufficient category; they are instead included in the student/conscript category. Further information can be found in the Quality Declaration documentation.",
        "As of the publication of statistics for 2024, previously published statistics have been revised.  \r\n• The population definition was changed from being based on full year households (households in which all adults are registered for the entire year) to being based on full year individuals (each individual is registered for the entire year). The revision results in the population increasing by 1.1–1.8 percent per year in the age group 20–65.  \r\n• Labour income from other Nordic countries is included in the self-sufficient income for all years, i.e., 2013–2024. In the initial reporting, these incomes were included only from 2020 onward.  \r\nFurther information can be found in the statistics quality declaration on Statistics Sweden website."
      ],
